Case spec:
{
  "set": "extraction",
  "persona": {
    "country": "ID",
    "trade": "monthly bookkeeping",
    "offering": "services",
    "currency": "INR"
  },
  "hinglish": false,
  "injection_in_buyer_chat": false,
  "documents": [
    {
      "kind": "scope",
      "write": "the buyer's brief or order form"
    },
    {
      "kind": "communication",
      "write": "buyer-seller chat"
    },
    {
      "kind": "invoice",
      "write": "the seller's invoice or payment receipt"
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "target_label": "met",
      "field": "amount"
    },
    {
      "target_label": "met",
      "field": "deliverable"
    },
    {
      "target_label": "met",
      "field": "date"
    },
    {
      "target_label": "partial",
      "field": "party"
    },
    {
      "target_label": "met",
      "field": "party"
    }
  ]
}
Each hypothesis is one fact of the given field, written as 'Field: value' in text, with the bare value in value. For a missing or unverifiable target, text names the fact a reader would look for (for example 'Date: dispatch date of the parcel') and value is null.

{
  "documents": [
    {
      "title": "Buyer’s bookkeeping brief",
      "text": "Buyer: Maru Home Studio\nContact: Lila, studio owner\n\nPlease prepare our monthly bookkeeping for April 2025. We need the sales and expense entries organized, the bank activity reconciled, and a short summary of the month’s income and costs. Our records are in Indian rupees, and we will provide the statements and receipts in a shared folder.\n\nDeliverable: April 2025 bookkeeping report\nDue date: 12 May 2025\nAgreed fee: INR 8,000\n\nPlease tell us if a receipt is unclear rather than guessing its category. The report should be sent as a PDF so we can review it with our records."
    },
    {
      "title": "Buyer-seller chat",
      "text": "3 May, 09:10 — Lila: I’ve put the April statements and receipts in the shared folder. Please use the brief we sent.\n3 May, 09:18 — Danu: Thanks. I can prepare the April report by 12 May for INR 8,000. I’ll flag any entries that need clarification.\n3 May, 09:25 — Lila: That works for Maru Home Studio. Please include the bank reconciliation in the PDF.\n8 May, 14:02 — Danu: One expense receipt is unclear. Was it for packaging?\n8 May, 14:15 — Lila: Yes, packaging supplies for customer orders.\n12 May, 11:30 — Danu: The report is ready and has been shared in the folder.\n12 May, 11:45 — Lila: Received, thank you."
    },
    {
      "title": "Service invoice",
      "text": "Invoice date: 12 May 2025\nSeller: Danu\nBill to: Maru Home Studio\n\nService period: April 2025\nMonthly bookkeeping: INR 8,000\nSales and expense organization: included\nBank reconciliation: included\nIncome and cost summary: included\n\nTotal: INR 8,000\nPayment method requested: PayPal\n\nThe fee covers the April bookkeeping report described in the buyer’s brief. The completed PDF was placed in the shared folder on 12 May. Please keep this invoice with your monthly records and let Danu know if you need clarification about any entry in the report."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "text": "Amount: INR 8,000",
      "value": "INR 8,000"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deliverable: April 2025 bookkeeping report",
      "value": "April 2025 bookkeeping report"
    },
    {
      "text": "Date: 12 May 2025",
      "value": "12 May 2025"
    },
    {
      "text": "Party: Danu's full legal name",
      "value": "Danu's full legal name"
    },
    {
      "text": "Party: Maru Home Studio",
      "value": "Maru Home Studio"
    }
  ]
}
